 think I think if there's  something to be on guard for it's that  it's that managing side way that was a  huge thing I never even thought about  that till I was about 15 years into my  career realized how many enemies I was  making of my peers because I was just so  focused on doing a good job and I felt  if I do a good job I'll get ahead I'll  be fine and I just wasn't focused on  those peer relationships like I should  have been it doesn't mean schmoozing and  all that it just means being aware of  what they're trying to do and what it  takes for them to be successful because  it's hard for it's hard for me to be  successful if the other units also are  even though I even though they don't  they're not my responsibility if I'm  thinking about the greater good they are  my responsibility  yeah they how do you gain the  credibility and trust of local  stakeholders and what are some of the  main big falls you've seen managers make  when meeting internationally for the  first time I think I think the biggest  challenge in working in another culture  which usually were talking about another  country but I know in my case even I saw  academia as another culture and it  really it really was almost like another  country you know to come here because of  just you know the way people think the  the things they value the way decisions  get made are different that's I think  the biggest mistake people make and  another culture is they make too many  assumptions they just assume that this  is the way people are thinking and  acting and behaving that it's they come  from their frame of reference years ago  the first time I was involved in Japan  for example it was very easy to make a  mistake that that the good English  speakers were the bright ones because  those are the ones you could connect  with they communicate with and we often  put the good English speaker in a job  when they really weren't the best for  that job and that's a kind of assumption  that you make that's really flawed and  so you make the assumption that because  someone's quiet they haven't got  anything to offer but in fact they have  a lot to offer you've got to find a way  to to bring them out so I think the  biggest mistakes are not taking the time  to understand the culture you never  fully understand those of you know that  and you never fully understand it but  you need to spend a huge of  at I'm listening so probably a mistake  out of the boxes you know too much  talking and not enough listening  particularly if you find yourself in  another culture I think that's that's  the biggest challenge and you know you  never can learn you'll never learn and  understand deeply another culture but so  I think partly is to recognize that and  to be quite humble about that and do  your best at listening a lot and trying  to figure out you know what is the value  system and the things going on in that  culture so that you might be more  effective anything else  Casey we got where you want to get yeah  thank you

